# allowed_signers for kubo-mcp release signatures (OpenSSH allowed_signers format).
#
# verify.sh checks mcp/release/dist/SHA256SUMS.sig against the keys listed here
# with `ssh-keygen -Y verify -n kubo-mcp-release`. One key per line:
#
#   <identity> namespaces="kubo-mcp-release" <keytype> <base64-public-key>
#
# Trust: a copy of this file that arrives in the same download as the archives
# proves nothing, because whoever replaced the archives could replace this file.
# Obtain the public key independently (the repository at a commit you trust,
# or from the maintainer) and pass it with `verify.sh --allowed-signers FILE`.
#
# Rotating keys: add the new key line first, release with the new key, then
# remove the old line once releases signed by it are no longer supported. To
# revoke a compromised key, delete its line and publish a new release; archives
# signed only by that key stop verifying. The first key line's identity is the
# default signer; override it with KUBO_MCP_SIGNER.
